      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This one has haunted me since the start of avatar 3.0.\n\nI believe this issue stems from the unity humanoid not being perfectly straight? You can preview the real viewball placement location by playing the default `proxy_tpose` animation on your avatar.\n\nI've been replacing the proxy animation and ever so slightly offsetting the RootT by x 0.006 for my avatar to compensate.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-02-18T23:12:54.644Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "All avatar's view point position (desktop, half body or full body) has their view point off center, GoGo Loco T Pose controller fixes this issue.\n\nThe black Mayu has the view point position centered using GoGo Loco T Pose controller.\n\nThe yellow Mayu has the view point off center using VRChat's default T Pose controller. Notice how it leans closer to one of the eye bones.\n\nThis can be observed with any avatar!",
